From 61f50e87ec27bef92cae735ba34cb7ba2c6ded3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rawdanger-recomp <rawdanger-recomp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:41:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rd: more pictures a second than 60 with frame generation (a
 limit, paced by the window)

- keys.ini fps_limit = 60 | 120 | 144 | 165 | 240 | none (PS2_FPS_LIMIT), Settings > Display > Pictures a second, the PC options row
- with frame generation on and a limit other than 60 (threads on), the game's presents only take its picture (after SMAA) into a
  store; the window thread shows pictures made from it at the limit's pace, each with the camera and bones of the moment by the
  clock (since the step's mark, a step lasting the real time between marks, smoothed)
- the pair of steps used is the one taken with the picture (a mark can come before its picture)
- Settings > Debug > Stats: pictures shown and from the game a second; the frame generation log: each paced picture's moment and
  the rates each second

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QNLFPekqhcU2dj7B3Utmea
